    "body": "Heyo! I'm interested in taking this issue on, I just have a quick question:\r\n\r\nDo you want the 'current with upstream' symbol to be shown if there are local, uncommitted changes too? Or only if the repo is completely up-to-date and there are no local changes? For example, if you have an untracked file but are up-to-date with your commits, it would show something akin to `[ lily/my-branch][?≡]`\r\n\r\nThanks, looking forward to helping out! :)",
