    "updated_at": "2021-07-31T22:22:42Z",
    "body": "The former please. Local uncommitted changes are controlled by their own symbol. What I want is if I have a remote-tracking branch configured that actually exists, and I'm not ahead or behind, then it should show the \"current with upstream\" symbol. Note that I can have a remote-tracking branch configured that doesn't exist; this should not show the symbol (it typically means the remote branch was deleted) as there's nothing to be current with.\r\n\r\nIn other words, if `git status --porcelain=2 --branch` includes the line\r\n\r\n```\r\n# branch.ab +0 -0\r\n```\r\n\r\nthen \"current with upstream\" should be shown.",
